        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2">
        
		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=37">
        	
		<font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Merilla</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Member</small></font>

        <br><img src=icon_star_blue.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_blue.gif border=0>
        <br>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>143 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="#c7b19c" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;22 Mar 2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 01:48:56</font>

        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=37"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=TopicQuote&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past"><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Let me begin by stating this is not a prelude to quitting. </P><P>After my temper tantrum tonight (and I apologize, folks), I began to realize that this isn't the same guild I've been a part of for the past two years.  Oh, it's the same in name, but with the exception of a scant handful of people, it hit me that I don't know most of you.  </P><P>Oh, sure we've chatted, but I don't really know what to expect of you when/if we do group.  It hit me after I did group with some of the "newer members" (newer to me, that is) that I am an outsider, while they seemed to know each other well.  And I'm not used to being an outsider in my own guild.</P><P>As I look through the roster (and it seems to me that many of these people are no longer with us), I was stunned to see that in just the warrior section alone, I know only two of the people personally, and one of those is ME.  Pogmo was right: I was thinking in the past for family--that group of people is long gone.  Even the officers I knew are gone. </P><P>Like I said, I'm not used to being an outsider in my own guild. I was upset this evening beause I'm not used to being left behind by Lore Keepers and then ignored.<BR>Perhaps this was just my interpretation, but <BR>I am not sure if this is what I should expect in the future.  I certainly hope not.<BR>I understand there was a timing issue--someone needed help for corpse retrieval.  I went LD during transport, and the group  waited around for a few minutes and I didn't show.  I tried to follow them all, not having the faintest idea of where they went, or how to get there...I spent a bit of time trying to find a way there, then gave up.  <BR>I felt unappreciated and unwanted, or, at least, disposable--after all, they had a better cleric, why did they need me? All of them were too busy to give me a tell until they were through.  </P><P>My feelings were hurt and I bitched it in guild chat. For that I apologize. I was upset<BR>and feeling a little put-out.  I spend many nights shouting for groups with no takers. <BR>When I finally get into a group, I get dumped--from a guild group, no less.</P><P>I am sure this is not going to be a normal occurance.  I want to group with you people again and try getting to know you. I'll try to have more patience in the future.</P><P>Okay, enough ranting and bitching.  Let's get together and do a massive raid so I can see some of you in action, please!</P><P>Merilla Vanilla Cleric 41<BR>Not just a young-in anymore!<BR>"Um--You gonna loot that?"</font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#ab8a69" valign="top">
        
		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=134">
        	
		<font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Shizue Osanowo</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Starting Member</small></font>

        <br>
        <br>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>20 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="#ab8a69" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;22 Mar 2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 02:27:21</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=134"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5197&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Well I don't know what went on Merilla.  But I too have felt that I really don't know the guild too well.  I would love to start by getting to know you in group play.  My shammy, although not part of the guild is 40, maybe we can get together to group sometime.  And as far as raids go, I have yet to go on a single raid since I have started playing.  The only one that went off, was in Dalnir, and I missed being able to go by one level.  So I am constantly seeking a way to be included on a guild raid.<BR>And always up for a chance to group with any Lore Keeper.</P><P>Shizue Osanowo</P><P> <a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#c7b19c" valign="top">
        
		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=62">
        	
		<font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Gartrin</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Member</small></font>

        <br><img src=icon_star_blue.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_blue.gif border=0>
        <br>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small> </small></font>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>194 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="#c7b19c" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;22 Mar 2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 09:46:44</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=62"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5201&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I do not know if this advice will help, hinder or is just not wanted, but i have found advice from the outside usually is helpful. I found myself not going on raids as well and for whatever reason it was, it made the game alot like i see written here. Lonely, alienating, and a "not want to" login. When i left to find new horizons i found a place that let the then young gartrin go on raids that he had no earthly reason for going on. Kedge keep raid at 34th the guild minimum was 40th. Ice worms at 35, minimum was 45, karnors castle at 32, minimum 40. The reason was afew fold. First and foremost its to project that the higher levels care about the lower levels. I KNOW the LK's do care but its another way to show hey, we want to show you what your missing. It also makes the lower level learn the way in which thier class operates in play and with others. I.E. I have become use to taking on situations that are above my head, it makes me a better player as i learn new skills to alter my surroundings and it butts me up next to 50+ levels that have been there to stop me from making mistakes or learning bad habits. Its no secret that i am being taught by afew of the best on the server. What is being taught is helpful to me, and to the guild and to the guild name should i go on a public raid.</P><P>Granted the Lk's are probabally not big enough to go raid a zone by themselves but you are big enough to take afew lower levels people into a zone and have fun with em. BTW, what it did for me was "supercharge" the desire to become a higher level, firm the reality that i am in a family, promote good will and burn into my head from where i came from and make the desire to repay the debt back to the lower levels. To take a person into battle that hasn't seen a high level mob or into a area they didn't know exsist is nothing short of a rush. The question of powerleveling comes into play then, "well we do not want to PL" fine, don't --- I wasn't and i went from 32 to 39 in 2 weeks. Granted the kedge raid i did get some exp but i was not on the pull team nor the KS team, i got 1.5 yellow in 3 hours due to getting lucky and operating as a team. 3 of the LK's were grouped with me that night --- Ask them how successful bringing a low level in can be.</P><P>LK's, you are a family with history in Norrath, your roots begin 2 years ago, the same time Eci went live. I remember the original LK's, i remember the name being created, the fledgling guild in peral and the guild coming out of harms way. I remember good people coming and going, i remember the good, bad and indifferent. YOU HAVE to do this on your own without outside influance at the meetings, you have to travel a road that will set afew peoples play time back for the better of a guild later. YOU HAVE to do it if you want to survive. You have a termendious leader at your disposal, one that is what i consider in the top 5 of best enchanters on the server. I know for a fact he is a good R/L human being and wants a family to lead and be lead by. Use him, listen to him, speak to him, you can do it and you can survive. </P><P></P><P>Gartrin Mezcrazie<BR>Enchanter of Eci<BR>Bounce bounce bounce<BR>Sylvan League<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#ab8a69" valign="top">
        
		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=77">
        	
		<font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Ealadan Azurefire</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Member</small></font>

        <br><img src=icon_star_blue.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_blue.gif border=0>
        <br>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>149 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="#ab8a69" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;22 Mar 2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 10:55:51</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=77"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="JavaScript:openWindow('pop_messengers.asp?mode=ICQ&ICQ=8041246&M_NAME=Ealadan+Azurefire')"><img src="http://online.mirabilis.com/scripts/online.dll?icq=8041246&img=5" height=15 width=15 alt="Send Ealadan Azurefire an ICQ Message" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5202&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Merilla let me say this again, I am sorry we went on while you were disconnected.  If it were not a situation in which we were in a hurry, I assure you, I would have waited twice the time that we did.  When we had finished killing the giant for Abyn's epic, Megadien had said over guild chat that he only had 1 hour before his corpse rotted, and it was somewhere in Droga, nobody knew.  Of course we were in a hurry because it is bad when anyone's corpse rots.  You were disconnected while we were zoning into Dreadlands, and we waited for 15 minutes at least.  We had to make a choice, and we did not want to risk Megadien losing his corpse and all of his equipment.  I'm sorry we had to leave you, and I'm sorry we couldn't stop to give you directions when you did log back on.  Kherl and Iinaru almost died because we got a little turned around in Frontier Mountains (I had the wrong loc to Droga), and we were in a bit of confusion for a few minutes.  It turns out we got Megadien's corpse back, thanks to the summoning abilities of Nerual.</P><P>As for not knowing people in the guild, I don't know what to tell you.  I've only been in the guild for a few months.  Before last night, I had never grouped with Merilla, Iinaru, Gereth, or Kherl.  I just met Abyn like a week ago.  This was the first time any of us had met Kherl.  If we seemed like we all knew each other for a long time, I can assure you we didn't, but we do know each other now.</P><P>And as for letting lower level people on higher level raids, nobody has ever asked.  As I look at the blackboard, I see at least 6 raids for the mid level LK.  A couple weeks ago when we were raiding CoM, we waited an hour for more lower level guildies to log on, but the only one under 50 who showed up was Daiyle.  When I was low level, I hated going on raids with higher level people.  It made me feel pretty bored... I like to have a challenge.  Somebody needs to pick up where Daiyle left off, and set up some raids for the lower level Lore Keepers.  If you need support from higher levels, just ask us, most of us would be thrilled to help.</P><P>Lastly, I applaud the communation we have had during the past couple days.  This is what the guild needs.  Let everyone know what is bothering you, and we can try to change it.  Just keep it constructive.</P><P>Again, Merilla, I am very sorry we left you last night.  I really do feel bad about it, but we all felt it was necessary under the circumstances.  I hope we get a chance to group again soon.</P><P>Ealadan Azurefire<BR>Keeper of Tears<BR>Eyes of Tunare<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#c7b19c" valign="top">
        
		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=10">
        	
		<font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Browso</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Grand Master of Lore</small></font>

        <br><img src=icon_star_gold.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_gold.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_gold.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_gold.gif border=0>
        <br>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>478 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="#c7b19c" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;22 Mar 2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 12:39:43</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=10"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="http://"><img src="icon_homepage.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Visit Browso's Homepage" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5207&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I would like to apoloigize for my little explotion yesterday here on the boards.</P><P>I dont know the full details of the CR or what happened last night.  But something to think of in the future is log off leaving a phone number with an in game friend. LK can find the corpse and get the cleric there, keep the area clear and call the dead person and pick it up from there. Either drag corpse to the zone or something but get you the rez. This may not have been possible with the offline time running out too. But its something to think about for the next time.</P><P>I too am very please with the new found flow of information. With out it we will wither and die. WE can not let that happen.</P><P>I agree with Ealadan, I personally would be bored on a high level raid as a lower level person. The mentoring part is truely an awsome idea. But if I died I would not be at all please and may place unwarranted blame on the higher ups for not protecting me. That is why level guide lines are placed on raids. They are not hard and fast, but guides for safety. I would only ever say no dont come if you are more than say 5 or 10 levels below the suggested range, depending on the make up of the raid (who is going)</P><P>Maybe I am not speaking this right or maybe I am wrong in my thinking.</P><P>Browso DaChoker</P><P>Maker of shiny trinkets<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#ab8a69" valign="top">
        
