        <td bgcolor="#ab8a69" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;22 Mar 2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 14:58:25</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=11"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5210&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Just a couple of thoughts.</P><P>Merilla, you could not be mean if you tried. Your voice is one that I miss greatly. I have felt what you feel. There were many times when I logged on and felt ike a stranger in my own family. All these new voices - and I did not know most of them. Add to that the beloved ones that were missing and I had a hard time for a while there. I found myself raiding with many of those new "voices" this weekend and it was a wonderful experience. Iinaru kept my sorry butt alive - and she is sweet as can be. Chakar did a great job - and is amazingly nice. Too many nice people to name, but you know who you are.<BR>All the new blood opens up so many possibilities. This guild has so much talent and so much energy. I look forward to seeing how it develops with all these ideas floating around out there.</P><P>A little perspective on raid limits:</P><P>It think much of it depends on the nature of the raid. Bringing a lower level on a higher level raid can endanger not only the lower level person, but the raid itself. When we do Vox raids, for example, we go in with a goal: to kill the flying white rat. We can take a limited number of people to try to control the lag. If the number of people must be limited, then you want the best possible people. You want the clerics with the best heal, the enchanter with the best shot at mez, the wizard with the best chance of having a  spell stick, the warrior able to do the best damage and stay standing long enough to make a  difference to the battle. The success of certain kinds of raids is totally dependent upon the levels of the people you bring. If you are hanging out with your guild just for fun, then great! Bring as many people as you can, use it as a chance to mingle the levels, get to know one another, learn from one another. If it is a "kill this thing or we all die" raid, then level limits are there for a good reason.</P><P>Just my rambling 2cp</P><P><BR>Dding-a-Lling<BR><a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

