        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5220&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I'll add my 2 cents from my experiences with the raid level limits in the past.  I remember the Burning Woods LK raid many moons ago.  I was level 32 and they said only level 35 could go.  No "ifs", "ands", or "buts".  I asked to go and was told I couldn't.  That turned me off quite a bit and contributed to my decision to leave.</P><P>I understand the Vox raids and such and issues with lag and limiting the number of players, but this was a case where there was an arbitrary level limit imposed.  All I wanted to do was go hunt with some friends and see a part of Norrath that I had never seen before.  If I died, then I died, but at least it was my decision.</P><P>You'll never see a level limit mentioned on a Nomadic Reveller raid.  We laugh at death and we laugh often!!!</P><P>But seriously, you may want to consider posting level limits as more of a guideline and allow lower levels to attend with the understanding that they do so at risk.  Just because YOU would be upset that YOU died doesn't mean everyone else has the same values.  Don't limit someone else's enjoyment of the game based on some pseudo-chivalrous decision.  You might not be doing them the favor you think you are.</P><P>Norbert Gearsmith<BR>Nomadic Reveller and one-time Lore Keeper<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

