        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5223&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I am sorry if I sounded like I was trying to gripe about level limits, this wasn't my intent.  What my gripe was about was the lack of activities scheduled for lower levels, other than by themselves.  For instance, the last guild meeting we had, everyone was supposed to bring their low levels, so that after we could raid split paw as a united guild.  Unfortunately this never happened.  I was the only low level there for the meeting.  Daiyle tried to promote activities in South Karana before his leaving the LK's, but even then, nobody supported them.  I did check many times.  And after a while all of this begins to wear on us who feel frustrated.  I am sorry, I didn't mean to detract from the original post from Merilla.  I just thought that it kinda fit in with her sense of not belonging to the guild as a viable member.  Oh and as goes the comment of PL, I have never asked anyone in my time playing to ever power level me, I think it robs the gaming experience, and this is not what I am asking for.</P><P>Shizue Osanowo</P><P> <a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
