        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5224&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Norbert I'll add my 2 cents from my experiences with the raid level limits in the past. I remember the Burning Woods LK raid many moons ago. I was level 32 and they said only level 35 could go.  </P><P><BR>I never let limits stop me from going anywhere....except to the Planes. (I still won't go there, yet!)  I remember those raids, I was level 24, but I'd get a ride and run my little tail off to the BW and holler for directions. (Is it paranoia when all those things really are out to get you?)  I grouped with Browso, Whacha and Ren in FM and got some awsome exp and a LOT of med time.  I didn't have a hefty heal, but I'd cast my mana out and rarely would anyone bite the big one.</P><P>The only thing I would suggest is that if you are a tad low for a grouping and you know where it's to be, research it--and make sure you are able to group and get the exp.</P><P>Do a test case with the group: run one kill that's blue for the highest level. If you get exp, stay with it.  You may not be able to blast it, so cast buffs, heals, try to tank, whatever....Do what you can to help. </P><P>Go for it.  The worst thing to happen is you find out your limitations.</P><P>Merilla Vanilla Cleric 41<BR>Not just a young-in anymore!<BR>"Um--You gonna loot that?"<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

