        <br>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font>
        <br><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>134 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="#c7b19c" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;22 Mar 2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 22:20:20</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=15"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="http://"><img src="icon_homepage.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Visit Whacha's Homepage" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5227&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I remember being in my low 30's, and hearing of the great battles happening in Vox's Lair, in Naggies Lair, and yes, even in the Planes. I longed to go and see these great beasts and the places that they dwelled. <BR>Then, a very dear friend in the guild sat down and spoke to me.<BR>These, were his words.<BR>He told me that he was proud of my skill as a warrior, but would I wish to cause others to die? I was a bit confused at his words and answered him truthfully. "No way" I stated. I then asked him what he ment.<BR>Basically, it came down to this. At my lvl at that time, I would have been a casualty waiting to happen. First off, I would be aggroing the creature more than most others, I would be taking more damage than the others, and would be loosing a higher percentage of my hitpoints quicker, thus making the healers spend more total mana, keeping a warrior alive that was only doing 1/3rd (if that) of the damage as the other warriors in the group. What would I be gaining out of this? Lost xp most likely.<BR>When can a lower lvl group with higher lvls?<BR>Quite often actually. <BR>Case in point. Group of us were in Karnors recently and Gartrin was well, being mezcrazy outside but I could tell he was rather bored. He was only lvl 32 at the time, but we needed some brain candy for our healers and casters. I spoke to the group and they all grinned, laughed, but then remembered the brain candy, and eagerly invited him to join the group. (all of us lvl 49+ highest being lvl 55) He wandered into karnors castle (a zone said to be lvl 46+ for tanks 49+ for casters) <BR>Then it happened... A dralvarg Sentry is Mezzed DONT TOUCH IT came scrolling up my screen. I stopped attacking, targeted the sentry and busted up laughing.. the little twerp had done it, he mezzed a lvl 50 creature. Yeah, ask browso what would have happened if the mez had broken.. we woulda been pealing that sucker off the floor, wall, and ceiling due to getting hit so hard, but he saved our kiesters and kept it mezed. It was the funniest thing I had seen in ages, until the next thing happened.. smack bang hit boom ouch (fight insuing) BOOM Gartrin has slain a Dralvarg Sentry.. not only had he mezzed it, he got the kill to LOL We kept a close eye on him the entire night, he had one, maybe two close calls, but all in all, we had a blast. It wasnt a raid though, it was a fun time at the zone to a dangerous zone, he aquired no xp.. or did he? He learned much, in the ways of grouping in a dangerous zone. And that, will save all of our lives i am sure of it, at a later date.<BR>Should lower lvls go on raids? NO.. Reason? They will most likely die, cause others to die, and become frustrated with the whole raid idea. <BR>Should they go on guild hunts yes they should. They should first off, become profficient at hunting in groups, learning to trust those in their groups. Lessons should be given (ie; Warriors, should take lower lvl warriors into the field of battle, even if it is against greens, and the secrets of the warrior trade should be shared, same with wizards, enchanters and such.) Warriors should learn to work with enchanters, as wizards should learn to work with warriors. Each class should practice using low lvl spells, and smaller weapons on low lvl creatures.. attack alot of them, and learn to work the best way to become proficient not at being the best in your class, but instead, at how to best compliment the other classes you are grouped with. <BR>I am called upon to assist with many raids now, is it because im the highest lvl warrior online? No way, my items, my ac, my skills are nothing compared to some of the warriors online. Why am I called? because I was instructed by some of the best out there, Teggo, taught me to fight with Druids, Lling taught me to fight alongside other warriors, Sirana, taught me to fight with an Enchanter, and my own wizard, taught me to fight with wizards.<BR>Each will enjoy the lust of combat within raids in their own time my friends, just be patient. Your time will come. Prepare though, and be the best that you can be. Learn to support the group your in in the best way you can, and you to will be on your way to great raids.</P><P>Whacha</P><P>I used to live here.<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
