        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=5232&TOPIC_ID=919&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=I%27ve+been+thinking+in+the+past&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Hi all,</P><P>I would like to make a few comments on raids and level limits, directed at no one that has posted, just my observations.</P><P>/incoherent ravings on</P><P>On raids into dungeons, unless you are being supervised (babysat) or have overwhelming odds, I think that levels do come into play. Keep in mind that your chances to effect an outcome in a battle relates directly to your level vs the NPC's. (this excludes healing, but it is effected by spells and mana pool availablilty)</P><P>As an example, my chance of landing a mez/charm/slow on a NPC is directly related to my level vs the mob. The tests done with relation to Charisma and Int and Wis all show a very minimal gain in succesful mez attempts, like 2 or 3 percent with 100 Charisma vs 200 Charisma. Where as level showes a significant gain in the ability to mez a NPC. This also applies to snaring, and rooting, where level is the key factor to getting the spell to stick. Ran into this alot with my druid on Quellious.</P><P>This also relates to resisting spells and other magical attacks. Take Sol A, those damn wizards see through invis, and seem to burn you down rather quickly. Also look at Droga some of the mobs there Harm Touch (oww!). This can change the course of a battle very quick. </P><P>I am sure all of you know this stuff when you go on a raid, but when someone dies due to a mob hitting them for full each round (heeh, the life of an enchanter), or an aggroed wiz bruns em down, the other people feel a little bad.</P><P>/incoherent ravings off</P><P>Kalene</P><P>Also, I am not discouraging low level (below the level expected for the dungeon) people go on raids, to the contrary I think it is good, and they should ask questions. As an example, Chakar and I work well together, we were in Lower Guk and I was rooting mezed mobs and was asked why, Chakar responded, I cannot taunt.</P><P><BR>Edited by - Kalene on 23 Mar 2001  11:37:32</P><P>Edited by - Kalene on 23 Mar 2001  11:40:23<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
